sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 85.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py; output: docs/media/pavement_cell_lobing_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0; spec_fingerprint: f1dc5c3feb4438b1986765273ee431fd638fbb88651110897b910ebc0100ae0a; artifact_sha256: c89ce769b8d1c86fc6395d1c4f9079b12b12f151c80d748245912b3c8001b8b1; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/arabidopsis_pavement_cell_specimen.jpg=4b7c1062f6ebfd6e..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/paper_citations.bib=b5d0bb17859e8dd0..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/pavement_cell_lobing_reference.json=de4e6daab5eae4a0..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/pavement_cell_shell_depth_reference.json=6d1aac5a29095651..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/scout_manifest.json=72c917ec10ac1a55...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sapala et al. (2018) eLife 7:e32794: outer periclinal cell wall tensile stress in pressurised FEM cell templates increases with the Largest Empty Circle radius (thin-wall proxy sigma_max ~ P R_LEC / h, Box 1 & Fig. 3); interdigitated puzzle lobing pins R_LEC near ~11.4 um as cell area expands to 4500 um^2 whereas isotropic polygonal/mutant cells grow as sqrt(A/pi) | Fu et al. (2005) Cell 120:687-700 & Lin et al. (2013) Curr Biol 23:290-297: antagonistic cortical ROP2-RIC4 (actin lobe outgrowth) and ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 (katanin-mediated microtubule neck bundling) polarisation in antiphase across shared anticlinal cell walls; lobeyness collapse in rop2 rop4 RNAi and ktn1/ric1 mutants | Armour et al. (2015) Plant Cell 27:2484-2500: lobe formation involves differential growth of periclinal and anticlinal walls in 3D (depth context; no amplitude-vs-depth table is used here); reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2D Euclidean Distance Transform R_LEC and ConvexHull solidity/lobeyness across A in [250, 4500] um^2 for a compact branched WT puzzle construction (band + alternating staggered finger lobes; aspect 2.6 at 4500 um^2), unlobed isotropic cells, ktn1/ric1 and rop2 rop4 mutants, and parallel-file monocot epidermis | 196-node periodic anticlinal boundary coupled ROP2-RIC4 / ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 reaction-diffusion PDE integrator (intracortical r = -0.9899, trans-wall r = 0.9998, 24.5 um lobe wavelength, exact intercellular area conservation) | (Pass 3) Reduced Foppl uniform-tension pressurised periclinal membrane solve -T lap(z) = P on the rasterised footprint with self-consistent tension T = T0 + E h eps/(1-nu), T0 = P H / 2, verified against the closed-form disk (0.9 %) and the inscribed-disk bound (18/18), used to TEST the LEC stress proxy: Pearson r(sigma_m, R_LEC) = 0.982 but fitted exponent 0.51 and isotropic/WT ratio 1.73 vs the proxy's 3.32 | (Pass 3) Depth-resolved anticlinal wall strip: outer-junction forcing by the ROP2-ROP6 wall displacement, Robin inner face (beta sweep 0 .. clamped), sparse FD Laplace solve vs modal closed form (1.2 %), dominant k = 8 mode inner/outer gain 0.028 (e^-1 penetration 4 um of H = 15 um), depth-distributed-forcing ablation (inner/outer 0.70) | Automated DoG + zero-compactness watershed segmentation of 10 interlocking puzzle cells from the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis leaf epidermis micrograph (mean S = 0.720, min S = 0.626; mean L = 1.316 in this environment vs 1.506 recorded by v2); transfer_boundary: The periclinal 'shell' is a uniform-tension membrane with an analytic clamped-edge bending boundary layer on the 2D footprint, not a bending-coupled 3D finite-element shell; E = 300 MPa, nu = 0.3, H = 15 um and T0 = PH/2 are order-of-magnitude assumptions (flagged in the vendored JSON), so the absolute stresses (34 vs 59 MPa) and the 1.73x ratio are model-conditional | The depth law (sinh/cosh modal attenuation) is a prediction of a prestressed-strip model verified against its own analytic solution; the inner-face anchoring beta = 2 is a modelling choice and no depth-resolved specimen measurement is vendored | The WT footprint is a deterministic geometric construction whose constants (lobe half-width 0.62 r_t, tip 1.25x, pitch 3.0 r_t, band fraction polynomial) were tuned to the vendored benchmark series, not grown by the spring-remodelling simulator of Sapala et al. (2018); the ROP2-ROP6 PDE does not feed the polygon; does_not_claim: Full 3D finite-element shell modelling of dome deflection coupled to anticlinal wall growth anisotropy, discrete microtubule stochastics, or any digitised amplitude-vs-depth measurement from confocal stacks]; other sources: Theory of Plates and Shells (2nd ed.) <https://archive.org/details/TheoryOfPlatesAndShells>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2004.12.026>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.01.022>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41477-019-0500-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.114.126664>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.32794> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.852"^^xsd:double .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "d58a084" .
}

